cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in a publication, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cgekit: a general toolkit for SAM-based computable general equilibrium models in Python"
abstract: >-
  Social accounting matrix handling and balancing, calibration, configurable nests and closures, CET and Armington trade, direct taxes, transfers and foreign ownership, within-period solution, recursive dynamics with several capital stocks and FDI, and welfare measurement, with base-year reproduction, homogeneity and Walras checks built in and an independent JuMP replica for validation.
authors:
  - family-names: "Moreira"
    given-names: "Gustavo Hoffmann"
    email: "gustavo@gakusai.net"
